  "result": "Perfect! The dates module is working correctly and integrated with createInvoice. Here's a summary:\n\n## Date Operations Module\n\n**Files created/modified:**\n\n1. **src/dates.js** - New module with three functions:\n   - `isValidDate(text)`: Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and checks calendar validity\n   - `addDays(date, n)`: Adds/subtracts days in UTC (handles month/year boundaries and leap years)\n   - `daysBetween(a, b)`: Returns whole days between dates (b - a), handling negative differences\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** - Updated to:\n   - Import `isValidDate` from dates module\n   - Remove local `isValidDate` function (now centralized)\n\n3. **test/dates.test.js** - New test file with 24 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Valid date validation (including leap years)\n   - Invalid formats and edge cases\n   - Day arithmetic across boundaries\n   - UTC timezone consistency\n   - Large date ranges\n   - Inverse relationships between functions\n\n**Key features:**\n- \u2705 All dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings everywhere\n- \u2705 All date arithmetic done in UTC, never local timezone\n- \u2705 Leap year handling (2000, 2004, 2024, etc.)\n- \u2705 Month/year boundary transitions\n- \u2705 Negative day calculations and date subtraction\n- \u2705 Consistent validation across createInvoice\n\n**Test results:** All 164 tests passing \u2713\n- 140 existing tests (customers, invoices, render, numbering)\n- 24 new date tests\n\nThe dates module provides a reliable, timezone-aware foundation for all date operations in the invoicing system.",
